## Verdict

**changes_requested -> `to-dev`.**

All four round-1 blocking findings are genuinely closed, by property rather than
by instance — I re-attacked each one with the exact mutants named in the round-1
verdict and every one is now killed. The implementation remains normatively
correct and every gate passes at the exact candidate tree.

It is rejected on four remaining Definition-of-Done evidence clauses. Four
production clauses can be individually disabled with the whole suite staying
green, and none of them is documented as subsumed. One of the four covers a
Section 3.2 **MUST NOT**, and one leaves Section 6.1 precedence layer 1
(command flags) completely undriven at the sole OS production entry point.

This is ordinary rework: no specification conflict, no platform constraint, no
human-only decision. The closure criterion in "Rework routing" below is bounded
and enumerable, so it terminates.

