| 1. Root-kind enforcement not derived per registry member | Skipping **each** of `data-root`, `state-root`, `cache-root`, `runtime-root` in `validateRootKinds` now reddens, each naming its own subtest. `TestLoadRefusesWrongOrUnreadableRootKinds` iterates `OverrideRegistry()`, so dropping any member from enforcement fails. 4/4 killed. |
| 2. Config-file regular-kind gate pinned only against a directory | `IsRegular` narrowed to `IsDir`, and separately widened to admit each of FIFO / socket / device / symlink, all redden. `fakeFileSystem` now synthesizes real mode bits. 5/5 killed. |
| 3. `LoadOS`/`OSInputs` 0% covered | `LoadOS` 100.0%, `OSInputs` 77.8%. Dropping the `ParsePlatform` guard in `OSInputs` reddens `TestLoadOSRefusesInvalidRuntimePlatformBeforeReadingOS`. The positive case drives `t.TempDir()` with all five `AX_*` set, so it does not depend on ambient state. |
| 4. §3.2 not-yet-created config path unimplemented | Implemented in `loadAbsentConfig`. Admitting an absent config without a parent check, skipping the parent `IsDir` check, collapsing parent stat failure into not-found, and forging `ConfigPresent` in **either** direction all redden. 5/5 killed. |
